Oh! Do hang him-we have waited
Many a day for such a chance;
Let the hempen cord be baited;
See how gracefully he'll dance
Dance on nothing! oh, how funny![…]

The brooks that sometimes run dry, or hide under the smooth stones;
In the time of fullness leaping from ledge to ledge down to the big brook that never dries;
Where the trout dart
